<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cuyamel Fruit Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1911–1929</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cuyamel Fruit Company was an American banana company founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-zemurray">Samuel Zemurray</a> in 1911, with plantations in the lower valleys of north-western Honduras near the Guatemalan border. It competed fiercely with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-fruit-company">United Fruit Company</a> for land, railway concessions and influence over Honduran governments until Zemurray sold it to United Fruit in 1929.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cuyamel-fruit-company.jpg" alt="Cuyamel Fruit Company" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Cuyamel Fruit Company Vector: Designism · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:House_flag_of_Cuyamel_Fruit_Company.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
